<!--
  THE STRING SURFACE, tranche 1: everything a wearer reads on the TextView
  paths — notices, bay titles and footers, row labels, the FIND panel.

  TRIMMED AT EXTRACTION (operator instruction, 2026-08-14): shorter labels both
  fit the instrument register and shrink what has to be translated and what has
  to fit a plate. Japanese runs ~1.5x the cap height of Latin (see L10n), so
  every character trimmed here is width bought for the JA build.

  NOT HERE, deliberately: callsigns, units, protocol tokens (SF7, dBm, CH0) —
  Latin in every locale per MeshmoreXR-i18n-ja.md §5. The stroke-font surfaces
  (HUD status, compass, node detail lines) also stay Latin: Glyphs cannot draw
  CJK and instrument codes read as codes.
-->
